[tool_result]Web search results for query: "heat pipe battery thermal management electric vehicle review 2024 2025 flat heat pipe vapor chamber"  Links: [{"title":"A review of thermal management systems of lithium-ion batteries used in electric vehicles - This section reviews heat pipe-based cooling battery thermal management systems (BTMS)","url":"https://jtte.chd.edu.cn/article/doi/10.1016/j.jtte.2025.06.002?viewType=citedby-info#7"},{"title":"A critical review on renewable battery thermal management system using heat pipes","url":"https://pure.seoultech.ac.kr/en/publications/a-critical-review-on-renewable-battery-thermal-management-system-/"},{"title":"Advances in battery thermal management systems and energy storage technologies - Skip to main contentSkip to article","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0735193326005713?dgcid=rss_sd_all#1"},{"title":"Two phase heat transfer approaches for battery thermal management: Current status, challenges and future outlook - The intersection of two-phase technologies aims to leverage the performance advantages of each to achieve optimal heat transfer ...","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2590123025018201#12#8"},{"title":"Flexible heat pipes in thermal management applications – A comprehensive review - Upon reviewing the applications for electronics cooling, it is clear that FHPs represent not merely an incremental improvement b...","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1364032125008408#7"},{"title":"Towards Efficient and Scalable Battery Thermal Management in Electric Vehicles: A Review of Technologies, Challenges, and Emerging Solutions - Towards Efficient and Scalable Battery Thermal Management in Electric Vehicles: A Review of Technologies, Challenges, and Emergi...","url":"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/11212315#1"},{"title":"A review of thermal management systems of lithium-ion batteries used in electric vehicles - A review of thermal management systems of lithium-ion batteries used in electric vehicles","url":"https://trid.trb.org/View/2633586#1"},{"title":"Advancements and challenges in battery thermal management technologies for electric vehicles; a systematic navigation on the latest trends","url":"https://www.mendeley.com/catalogue/79106c89-aafc-3ef2-bed2-765aedb770bc/"},{"title":"A review of power battery cooling technologies. - Use this link to get back to this page","url":"https://go.gale.com/ps/retrieve.do?tabID=T002&resultListType=RESULT_LIST&searchResultsType=SingleTab&retrievalId=cc8d281e-13ad-4c74-8b32-3c60c1a25464&hitCount=3&gtmSearchId=3d960aa0-7f9e-478f-bb33-e12f41cc06c5&searchType=AdvancedSearchForm&currentPosition=3&docId=GALE%7CA828849367&docType=Report%2C+Brief+article&sort=Relevance&contentSegment=ZONE-Exclude-FT&prodId=AONE&pageNum=1&contentSet=GALE%7CA828849367&searchId=R1&userGroupName=anon%7E7b76300a&inPS=true#1"},{"title":"Advanced Battery Cooling in Electric Vehicles: A Review of Phase Change Material and Heat Pipe Integration - 图书馆订阅： Guest","url":"https://www.dl.begellhouse.com/cn/references/587c7d3679ede81c,2ef0b2e331dc56a8,3a1e991d00c4606e.html#1"}]  # Heat Pipe Battery Thermal Management for Electric Vehicles – Summary of 2024–2025 Reviews  ## Overview  Recent reviews (2024–2025) consistently identify heat pipes as a promising thermal management technology for lithium-ion batteries in electric vehicles (EVs), both as a standalone passive solution and as a key component of hybrid systems (e.g., combined with liquid cooling, air cooling, or phase change materials, PCMs). The consensus is that hybrid configurations deliver the best balance of peak-temperature control and temperature uniformity.  ## Key Findings on Heat Pipe Performance  - **Flat heat pipes** paired with heat sinks are reported as one of the best passive methods for keeping battery temperatures below 50 °C, with a ~30% reduction in heat sink thermal resistance. Water-cooled heat pipes maintain cell temperatures below the permissible 55 °C range at 25 °C intake temperature and 1 L/min flow rate. - Heat pipes with thermal conductivity approaching 90× that of copper can reduce battery peak temperatures by 10–25 °C (PCM-based systems achieve 5–20 °C reductions, and hybrid PCM+heat pipe designs can reach reductions up to 46.1 °C with temperature differentials kept below 5 °C). - A 2025 review (Deshmukh et al., IHMTC-2025) emphasizes that exceeding 50 °C reduces capacity and charging efficiency, while cell-to-cell gradients above 5 °C accelerate degradation and thermal runaway risk — directly motivating heat pipe and hybrid integration.  ## Structural and Hybrid Configurations Reviewed  - **Flat heat pipe + aluminum plate** (prismatic cells): effective under forced convection; low thermal resistance heat pipes with forced convection perform best. - **U-shaped micro heat pipes + air cooling** (Ren et al., 2021): active cooling with U-shaped heat pipes gave the best cooling performance; passive cooling without heat pipes performed worst, though it provided the most homogeneous temperature. Hybrid air+heat pipe systems are viable, but increased airflow raises fan power consumption and reduces homogeneity. - **Liquid cooling + heat pipes** (Jang et al., 2022): hybrid systems (heat pipes on sides and bottom) improved lower-region cooling and temperature homogeneity versus pure liquid cooling; discharge rate affects temperature more strongly than fluid or ambient temperature. - **Heat pipe + PCM hybrids** (Hu et al., 2022, using R134A in U-shaped plate heat pipes with eicosane PCM): transferred nearly all heat at 3C discharge; more effective in providing homogeneity at high discharge rates. - **PCM + heat pipe variants** reviewed include oscillating heat pipes (OHPs), micro heat pipes (MHPA kept battery temperature within 40 °C), 3D pulsating heat pipes, and PCM-foam-heat pipe hybrids (up to ~59.9% temperature reduction during charging with fan assistance). - **Flexible/branch heat pipes** (2025 review): Y-shaped flexible branch heat pipes (polyurethane tubes, copper mesh wick, deionized water) reached thermal resistance as low as 0.47 °C/W and maximum heat transport of 25 W; squid-inspired pulsating heat pipes with Teflon branches and acetone achieved effective conductivity of 6750 W/(m·K) — 17× copper — with ~10–13% performance loss at 90° bends. The authors note these are at Technology Readiness Levels 4–5, i.e., laboratory-stage.  ## Classification and Trends  - 2025 reviews systematically categorize BTMS into active (air, liquid, immersion), passive (PCM, heat pipes), and hybrid strategies. Heat pipe-based cooling is highlighted as a "frontier" solution alongside nanofluid cooling, intelligent thermal materials, and AI-based dynamic management. - Multi-objective optimization (cooling performance vs. weight, power consumption, cost, environmental impact) and vehicle-level control strategies are identified as urgent research needs. - Emerging directions include microencapsulated PCMs, nanofluid-assisted heat pipes, machine learning for thermal state prediction and control, and AI/CFD surrogate modeling.  ## Caveats  The provided results address **flat heat pipes** extensively but contain little specific discussion of **vapor chambers** as a distinct technology; vapor chamber performance data would need to be sourced from additional literature. Heat pipe effectiveness is strongly dependent on wick structure, working fluid, configuration, and operating conditions, and extended research is still required for safe, practical deployment in daily EV use.   REMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.
